WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.602 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:06.605
-Hey, everybody.
Welcome to "Corrections."

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:09.743
August. End of August.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.278
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.615
I said "Cinnabun."
It's Cinnabon.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.116
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.218
I've often got that wrong,
and I looked it up,

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.854
and I guess one of the reasons
they went with Cinnabon

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:25.025
is because "bon"
is French for "good."

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:29.028
And if you've ever been
in LaGuardia

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.364
holding a Cinnabon,

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.199
I think you've probably thought,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:36.035
"This is how the French eat."

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.870
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.239
Speaking of LaGuardia,

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:43.242
I said it would be a good
pangram on Spelling Bee.

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:45.578
I was told by a bunch
of Spelling Bee fans,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.480
no, pangrams --

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.284
Spelling Bees do not accept
proper nouns.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.418
Also --

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:56.422
a lot of LaGuardia-themed errors
this week, guys.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:01:00.259
I talked about flying direct
from LaGuardia to LAX.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:06.599
There's no flight direct
from LaGuardia to LAX...

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:10.770
because LAX won't allow
flights from LaGuardia to land.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.773
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.274
But then we showed a ticket,

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:17.610
like a hypothetical ticket

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.613
for my nonexistent
LaGuardia flight.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.449
And the flight number
was NY2356.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:25.785
Multiple people said

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:29.021
that would be
an Iceland Air flight

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:32.859
from Reykjavik to Egilsstadir.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:36.696
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.866
You have jackal hearts,

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:43.369
jackal brains,

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.539
eagle eyes.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:52.845
I mean, what would a jackal with
eagle eyes even look like?

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:56.182
I guess like this.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.284
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.058
Not available anywhere.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:11.797
I talked about how when I do
my Vince Vaughn impression,

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:13.132
it has to be three "buddies."

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.468
Buddy, buddy, buddy --
that's Vince Vaughn.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.537
And that if you add a buddy,
it's no longer Vince Vaughn.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.873
It would be anybody when you go,
"Buddy, buddy, buddy, buddy."

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.508
Some people said
that's actually --

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:24.844
now you're doing Twiki,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.780
the robot from
"Battlestar Galactica."

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.615
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.784
Buddy, buddy, buddy, buddy.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.788
Not the new "Battlestar,"
the orig-- the classic,

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.456
the 1978 "Battlestar,"

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:39.458
which Shoemaker and I
always talk about.

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:42.795
The best special effects.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.764
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.266
Timeless.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.100
Watch it now,
it's not dated at all.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.605
And, I hate to say it...

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.106
no offense to
the big guy upstairs,

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:59.111
but when you ask me who my
favorite Canadian Lorne is...

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:00.780
Lorne Greene.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.114
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.850
Close number two.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.184
The great Lorne Greene.

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.685
But now I think you...

00:03:06.685 --> 00:03:08.788
Now, after somebody's
made this --

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.423
buddy, buddy, buddy, buddy.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.258
Like, now I want
a remake of "Battlestar"

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.294
with Owen Wilson as Starbuck

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:18.964
and Vince Vaughn as Twiki.

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.666
[as Wilson] Hey, I think
that girl over there

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:21.800
is looking at me.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.102
[as Vaughn]
Buddy, buddy, buddy, buddy.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.637
[as Wilson] She's a Cylon?!

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.638
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.040
Wow!

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.810
[Normal voice] Alright,
so, like two weeks ago,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.145
we made a knitting --

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.148
you know, we basically conflated
knitting and crochet.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:39.818
And then last week, I guess,
maybe even two weeks ago,

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:42.655
I read a comment -- a very
foul-mouthed comment

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.924
from someone
in the knitting community.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.626
And then my observation was,
"Well, I guess my stereotype

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:49.128
was wrong about knitters."

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:54.466
I did not think that they were
prone to cursing.

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:57.135
Based on saying that,

00:03:57.135 --> 00:04:01.140
I caught a world of hell.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.842
And I should say,
what happened was

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.677
it seemed like a very popular --

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.013
a very nice woman who seems to
be of the knitting community.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.182
She clipped out just me
talking about knitting

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:13.185
from "Corrections," and I cannot
stress this enough --

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:16.355
"Corrections" is meant
to be seen as a whole.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.324
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.126
Ideally, you have to watch
all of them.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:26.299
If you're coming in late,
you're missing so much.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.801
So, anyways, I guess she posts,
like, you know,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.803
"Here, this Seth Meyers thing
is about knitters."

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.139
And they have come after me.

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.474
And so I would say now
about knitters --

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:36.642
here's my new stereotype.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:39.812
You are of various --
you are of all ages,

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.313
curse like sailors,

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:44.250
don't have a great sense
of humor about knitting jokes.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.685
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:48.020
But it's so funny because I
think people often say, like,

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:52.859
"Oh, you must get so much
negative feedback from people

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.827
based on the kind
of show you do."

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.829
And I will say,
this is the truth,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:05:00.833
it's not MAGA people,
it's not anti-vaxxers --

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:04.870
the two worst [bleep] storms
we've ever had at this show

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:10.042
are knitters/crocheters

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:13.379
and the marching band
community.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.548
Do you remember when we made
a joke about marching band?

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:19.385
It was so bad, Shoemaker and I
had to live upstate.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.721
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:27.226
Those are the people --
marching band and knitters.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.728
I do not --
I wish you no ill will.

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:32.064
I do not want trouble,
'cause I'm very --

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:34.733
I'm very confident at this point
that my last breath will be,

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:37.136
I'll just be lying in bed
and I'll hear like --

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.404
♪ Ba ba-ba-ba bum-bum ♪

00:05:39.404 --> 00:05:42.742
and then just take, like,
a knitting needle to the eye,

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.077
like, Moe Greene style.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:47.380
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:57.390
I said as soon as I was
able to get the vaccine,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.059
I lined up.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.794
I was told by somebody
you cannot --

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:05.131
one person cannot line up.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.966
You have to -- It's a plural.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.301
It has to be a plurality
of people to line up.

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:11.637
And when you're one person,
you can either get in line

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.472
or you can join a line.

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:16.809
No man -- it's the classic
John Donne poem.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.978
No man is a line.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.979
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:22.815
That's for the --
[ Laughs ]

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:26.819
That's for our
Spelling Bee people.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.655
So, I talked about
there's no left-handed flutes.

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:33.425
And there's some, but they're
very hard to get

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:34.760
and they're expensive.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.763
And I thought,
I was even hopeful

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:40.933
that it was just prejudice
against left-handed

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.602
monster people.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:43.602
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:44.904
But it's not.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:46.405
Somebody said, like,
"Well, think about it."

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:47.740
If you're in an orchestra,
you can't --

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.742
they all have to --
if people are sitting,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.911
they all have to go
the same way.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:55.915
'Cause if I'm going this way
and then it's like this...

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.084
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.925
I said last week that
something was an homage

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:10.596
to...

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:15.267
Johnny Two Times
in "Goodfellas."

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:18.103
It's Jimmy Two Times.

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:22.441
Now I'm worried
I have it wrong again.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:25.243
I think it's right.
The problem is, for me,

00:07:25.243 --> 00:07:29.415
I saw a director's cut

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.083
where, you know,
it's the famous scene

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.252
where Ray Liotta, his character,

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:36.755
which I think was...
I think Ray Liotta.

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:38.758
I think he played himself.

00:07:38.758 --> 00:07:39.826
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:41.260
And he's going through
and he's like,

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.262
"There was Jimmy Two Times,
who was called that

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:44.763
'cause he said
everything twice --

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:46.432
'I'm gonna get the papers,
get the papers' --

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.167
and then his brother
Johnny Two Times,

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.501
who also said
everything twice --

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:50.836
'I'm gonna get the peppers,
get the peppers.'"

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:53.506
And they cut that,

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:56.541
'cause I think even Scorsese was
like, "This is redundant."

00:07:56.541 --> 00:07:59.712
But that's what I saw,
so that's why I got it wrong.

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:03.882
We've been talking about --

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:06.385
made a joke about a Walmart
in Astoria.

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:09.688
There was no Walmart in Astoria,
then people in Oregon said,

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:12.858
"There is a Walmart
in our Astoria."

00:08:12.858 --> 00:08:15.861
And then other people said,
no, that's in Warrenton.

00:08:15.861 --> 00:08:17.696
It should be noted
there is an airport

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:21.200
called the Astoria Airport,
also in Warrenton.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.371
But a little fun fact
I found out is,

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:28.373
you know what movie they filmed
in Astoria?

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:30.376
"Goonies."

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.712
Do you remember "Goonies,"
Shoemaker?

00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:34.713
It was good.

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:37.049
It was good enough.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:38.751
It's good enough for me.

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:40.386
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:45.257
A lot of fun characters
in "Goonies."

00:08:45.257 --> 00:08:47.260
Sloth -- do you remember
how Sloth talked?

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:50.729
He would --
I'm not gonna do Sloth.

00:08:50.729 --> 00:08:53.566
Can't do Sloth anymore.

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:56.902
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.902 --> 00:08:59.972
Can't believe Sloth was even
allowed to be in a movie,

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.306
but that's 1985.

00:09:01.306 --> 00:09:05.477
You can't go onstage
and do Sloth.

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:06.979
"Don't do Sloth" --

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:09.482
the motto at impression camp.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:10.649
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.649 --> 00:09:12.818
It's on the wall.

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:14.319
Don't do Sloth.

00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:16.155
It's in Latin.

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:17.656
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.656 --> 00:09:19.158
So you have to ask.
You're like, "Wha?"

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:20.660
And they're like,
"Don't do Sloth."

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.328
You're like, "From 'Goonies'?"
They're like, "Yeah, yeah."

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:26.832
Don't do Sloth.

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:28.700
Liked rocky road.
I can tell you some fact--

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:32.705
Liked rocky road, Baby Ruth,
loved Chunk.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.879
Rudy would make a good Sloth.

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.146
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:44.150
[as Giuliani] Baby Ruth?

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.319
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:51.657
[Normal voice]
Speaking of impressions camp...

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:55.627
I said that when I did my
Matthew McConaughey,

00:09:55.627 --> 00:10:00.132
my counselor at impression camp
hung himself.

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:03.134
A lot of people said,
"Hanged himself."

00:10:03.134 --> 00:10:07.139
Which then made me feel awful
because I know the diff--

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:09.908
He didn't hang himself.

00:10:09.908 --> 00:10:12.878
He was m-- He gets upset.

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:15.381
Like, he doesn't like
when we do McConaughey,

00:10:15.381 --> 00:10:17.383
'cause he thinks it's hacky.

00:10:17.383 --> 00:10:20.552
And I did it during camp
at impression camp

00:10:20.552 --> 00:10:22.887
and he does this really
passive-aggressive thing

00:10:22.887 --> 00:10:24.389
where he takes a chair

00:10:24.389 --> 00:10:26.725
and then he goes over
to the coat rack

00:10:26.725 --> 00:10:29.895
and just get--
he, like, hangs like this.

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:31.797
Just, like,
by the back of his coat.

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:33.466
And then he kicks the chair over
and he's like,

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:35.468
"Leave me here."

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:37.469
[ Laughter ]

00:10:37.469 --> 00:10:40.472
And...
[ Laughs ]

00:10:40.472 --> 00:10:41.974
And then I'm like, "What?"

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:44.143
And he goes, he's just like,
just such a...

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:45.144
[mouthing words]

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:46.311
He's a dick.

00:10:46.311 --> 00:10:47.546
He's like, "Just leave me here.

00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:49.715
I don't wanna do this anymore."

00:10:49.715 --> 00:10:53.885
And I'm like, "Well, what?
What should I say to everybody?"

00:10:53.885 --> 00:10:55.788
And he's like,
"Say I hung myself."

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:57.756
And I was like,
"Well, don't you think

00:10:57.756 --> 00:10:59.625
that some people may think
you, like" --

00:10:59.625 --> 00:11:01.627
And he's like,
"That's 'hanged'!"

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:03.295
[ Laughter ]

00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:04.696
They're bad -- He's a bad guy.

00:11:04.696 --> 00:11:06.398
Like, I feel like I've talked
about impression camp

00:11:06.398 --> 00:11:08.234
and, like, made it seem,
like, really fun,

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:10.068
but they're awful.

00:11:10.068 --> 00:11:12.738
The counselors there, they just,
like, drill you, drill you!

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:14.573
You're like, "I -- W--
Need more cowbell."

00:11:14.573 --> 00:11:16.074
They're like, "Again!"
"Cowbell."

00:11:16.074 --> 00:11:17.376
"Again!"

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:19.378
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.378 --> 00:11:21.981
"I gotta fever."
"Again!"

00:11:25.283 --> 00:11:28.453
What else?

00:11:28.453 --> 00:11:32.591
You know, this is -- this is
the last "Corrections"

00:11:32.591 --> 00:11:34.593
during Emmy voting.

00:11:34.593 --> 00:11:38.564
And I don't -- I want
to make something clear.

00:11:38.564 --> 00:11:43.902
I, uh -- I don't want an Emmy
for this.

00:11:43.902 --> 00:11:45.738
I need it.

00:11:45.738 --> 00:11:47.473
[ Laughter ]

00:11:51.409 --> 00:11:53.746
Sometimes I lash out,

00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:55.747
I lash out during "Corrections."

00:11:55.747 --> 00:11:58.083
but there is...

00:11:58.083 --> 00:12:02.754
there is a reason for that,
which is, um...

00:12:02.754 --> 00:12:05.757
Well, I think, um...

00:12:05.757 --> 00:12:09.695
I think Christopher Walken
said it best.

00:12:09.695 --> 00:12:12.031
-'Cause every once in a while,

00:12:12.031 --> 00:12:16.368
the lion has to show the jackals

00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:19.238
who he is.

00:12:19.238 --> 00:12:21.706
-Okay.

00:12:21.706 --> 00:12:24.043
I think that's everything.

00:12:24.043 --> 00:12:26.378
[ Laughter ]

00:12:26.378 --> 00:12:30.082
And that's...it.

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:34.754
We will see you all
in September.

